   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Verbs that take «être»",
     "texto": [
      "A few verbs, almost all of movement, form the past with **être** instead of «avoir»: **Je suis allé** (I went, I have gone).",
      "The most important: **aller** (to go) → allé, **venir** (to come) → venu, **arriver** (to arrive) → arrivé, **partir** (to leave) → parti, **rester** (to stay) → resté, **sortir** (to go out) → sorti, **entrer** (to come in) → entré.",
      "All reflexive verbs also take «être»: **Je me suis levé** (I got up)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Agreement",
     "texto": [
      "With «être», the past participle agrees with the subject, like an adjective. If a woman is speaking: **Je suis allée**. In the plural: **Nous sommes allés**; if they are all women: **Nous sommes allées**.",
      "You can hardly hear it when speaking, but you must write it."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
